# Allowlist, not a denylist.
#
# Everything is excluded first and only what the image build needs is added back, so a
# new file in this repo cannot leak into a public image by being forgotten here. That
# matters more than usual: vendor-freetoken/ carries a .git pointing at a personal fork,
# docs/ contains host paths, and target/ is 40 GB of build artifacts.
*

!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!build.rs
!src
!docker
!web

# Re-excluded even inside the allowlist above; last match wins.
**/.git
**/.env
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/id_ecdsa*
**/id_ed25519*
**/id_rsa*
**/.netrc
**/*.log

# The image builds its own frontend in a Node stage; a local node_modules or dist would
# only add unused, possibly stale bytes to the build context.
web/node_modules
web/dist
